|lore=“Looks like somebody’s beginning to take an interest in your handiwork.” Imperial stormtroopers coerce local residents to assist them in the apprehension of Rebel scum.
|game_text=At the beginning of your battle phase, use 1 Force to initiate a battle between two Imperials and an opponent’s character present at same interior site. For remainder of turn, no other battles may occur here and opponent takes no battle damage here.
|printings={{Card versions/Local Trouble (Premiere)}}
|errata_history=The Players Committee first published this Virtual card on an old-style slip (before its December 2006 remaster of the set). The sheet copy that survives is the February 2003 re-issue PDF; the date of the first release is unknown (the sheet gives the legal date 1 June 2002). Icons printed on the slip are written here in brackets ([Pilot], [Immune to Alter], [Immune to Sense], [Immune to Control]); ▲ and ▼ are printed as such. Versions of the Virtual Original card, in date order:
* '''Original''' ([[Local Trouble (V) (Virtual Set 2)]]): the Players Committee's Virtual Set #2 sheet (PDF made 3 February 2003, a February 2003 re-issue; legal date on the sheet 1 June 2002; first release date unknown). Full text: “Use 1 Force at the beginning of your battle phase to allow any two Imperials at an interior site to battle any one opponent's character (your choice); opponent suffers no battle damage here. No other battles may occur at this site this turn.”
* '''PC-E1''' (this page): the Players Committee remaster sheet (Virtual Set 2: Our Most Desperate Hour, official text as of 4 December 2006). Full text: “At the beginning of your battle phase, use 1 Force to initiate a battle between two Imperials and an opponent’s character present at same interior site. For remainder of turn, no other battles may occur here and opponent takes no battle damage here.” '''What changed:''' “Use 1 Force at” → “At”; “phase” → “phase, use 1 Force”; “allow any” → “initiate a battle between”; added “and an opponent’s character present”; “an” → “same”; “site to battle any one opponent's character (your choice);” → “site. For remainder of turn, no other battles may occur here and”; “suffers” → “takes”; removed “No other battles may occur at this site this turn.”.
|sources=* [https://web.archive.org/web/20071024153738/http://www.swccgpc.com/Resources/VirtualCards2.pdf#page=4 VirtualCards2.pdf] (Players Committee Remaster sheet, Internet Archive 24 October 2007) — official text as of 4 December 2006; page 4, slip 41. Slip image and game text from this sheet.
* Lore and art: the printed Decipher card, [[Local Trouble]].
* Full-card remaster: [[Virtual Set 2: Our Most Desperate Hour#Cards|Virtual Set 2: Our Most Desperate Hour]] (fan reconstruction, 2026).
|hatnote=Earlier versions of this Virtual Original card: [[Local Trouble (V) (Virtual Set 2)]]. For the Decipher card this slip modifies, see [[Local Trouble]]. Code OVS2 · GEMP id 1102_41.
}}

